==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|Tamesis|lang=la}}, ultimately of {{etyl|cel|en}} origin. The letter ''h'' was mistakenly inserted later, as if the word was derived from Greek and had θ in it. The pronunciation, though, did not change to /θ/.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR| tĕmz}}, {{IPA|/tɛmz/}}
* {{audio|en-uk-Thames.ogg|Audio (UK)}}
* {{audio|en-us-Thames.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# [[river|River]] in South [[England]] flowing 336 [[km]] (209 [[mile|mi.]]) through [[London]] to the [[North Sea]].
# [[river|River]] in [[Ontario]] province, [[Canada]], flowing 258 [[km]] (160 [[mile|mi.]]) to Lake [[St. Clair]].
# [[estuary|Estuary]] in the U.S. State of [[Connecticut]] flowing 24 [[km]] (15 [[mile|mi.]]) past [[New London]] to [[Long Island Sound]].

